Package: hd-desktop
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: hd-base, hd-art, hd-fonts, python3, python3-jinja2, sudo, dconf-cli,
 greetd, uwsm, dbus-user-session, desktop-base,
 hyprland, hyprland-qtutils, hyprpaper, hypridle, hyprlock, hyprshutdown,
 kitty, wofi, mako-notifier, libnotify-bin, libglib2.0-bin, jq,
 pipewire, wireplumber, pulseaudio-utils, wiremix, playerctl, brightnessctl,
 grim, slurp, swappy, wl-clipboard,
 nwg-look, qt5-gtk-platformtheme, qt6-gtk-platformtheme,
 audacious, mpv, imv, firefox, meld, yazi
Recommends: hd-screensaver
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian desktop
 Depends on the packages of the HyprDebian desktop, so that they are
 installed with it and stay installed: Hyprland with uwsm, hyprpaper,
 hypridle and hyprlock, greetd, kitty, wofi, mako, PipeWire, the screenshot
 tools, the GTK and Qt themes, and the desktop applications.
 .
 greetd logs the first user in to Hyprland on tty7 at the boot; the user is
 the key hd-desktop of /etc/hyprdebian/config.json, written into
 /etc/greetd/config.toml by hd-desktop-render. The package also installs the
 files that new users get in /etc/skel: the configs of Hyprland, hypridle,
 hyprlock, hyprpaper, kitty, mako, wofi, mpv, PipeWire and nwg-look, and the
 commands that the key bindings run: the reboot and power off questions, the
 monitor mode menu, the mount menus and the volume keys. It recommends the
 screensaver of hd-screensaver, which hypridle starts.
 The users in the group sudo mount and unmount drives from the mount menus
 without a password.
